afmf-linux (1.3.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed: device-level commands resolved through vkGetInstanceProcAddr are hooked only where
    the driver has them; a game submitting from several threads no longer serialises on the
    layer; the layer's queue is never protected; vkCreateDevice retries with the game's own
    request when the layer's additions fail.
  * Fixed: the governor paces one-in-n on the frame's own number; AFMF_MIN_FPS clears with a
    margin instead of flickering generation; the pacing hold has a minimum with pacing on and
    a 40 ms ceiling.
  * Fixed: the HDR luma is clamped before it is stored as a byte; the half-resolution downscale
    samples against the frame's size.

 -- Lain <lain@digitalexperiments.dev>  Tue, 22 Sep 2026 21:40:00 +0200

afmf-linux (1.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Changed: the optical flow and the block search follow the resolution by default instead of
    always asking for the most. From 1440p up the flow runs at half resolution with five pyramid
    levels, which costs 578 us per generated frame at 3440x1440 where the previous defaults cost
    716. AFMF_PERFORMANCE_MODE=quality AFMF_SEARCH_MODE=high keeps the previous behaviour.
  * Changed: at half resolution the game's frame is read once, as full resolution already did,
    instead of being copied and the copy downscaled.
  * Fixed: the block search no longer writes a row or column of motion vectors outside the flow
    image on pyramid levels whose size is not a multiple of sixteen.

 -- Lain <lain@digitalexperiments.dev>  Tue, 22 Sep 2026 20:15:00 +0200

afmf-linux (1.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed: the block search keeps a vector only with evidence behind it. A block whose picture
    carries no detail (fog, snow, sky) used to inherit the coarse level's guess and warp the
    background with it, smearing moving silhouettes; it now stores the zero vector.

 -- Lain <lain@digitalexperiments.dev>  Tue, 22 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0200

afmf-linux (1.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed: AFMF_DUMP_DIR creates the directory it names instead of writing nothing when it does
    not exist, writes 10-bit swapchains as well as 8-bit ones, and logs what it cannot write.

 -- Lain <lain@digitalexperiments.dev>  Tue, 22 Sep 2026 17:00:00 +0200

afmf-linux (1.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed: GPU hang on Intel (ANV). The block search's cross-subgroup sums and minimums now
    combine every subgroup the driver chose instead of exactly two of 32 lanes, and the scene
    change detector completes before the coarsest search instead of alongside it.
  * Fixed: the scene change detector's shared-memory reductions ran their last steps without
    barriers, which only holds on subgroups of 32 lanes or more; on Intel's 8- and 16-lane
    subgroups the result was wrong. Generation now checks the device's subgroup operations
    (basic, arithmetic, quad in compute) and the r8ui/rg16i storage formats before starting.

 -- Lain <lain@digitalexperiments.dev>  Mon, 21 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0200

afmf-linux (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Quality defaults: optical flow at display resolution with all seven pyramid levels and
    blended fallback, at the cost of the old half-resolution default, because a block whose
    vector from the coarser level already matches skips the search (AFMF_STATIC_BLOCK_SAD).
  * A FIFO swapchain is created in MAILBOX when the surface offers it (AFMF_PRESENT_MODE):
    the doubled presents no longer each take a refresh slot.
  * HUD detection (AFMF_HUD_DETECT); direct output into the swapchain image
    (AFMF_DIRECT_OUTPUT, opt-in).
  * Governor under GPU contention (AFMF_GOVERNOR) and AFMF_MIN_FPS; pre-recorded command
    buffers; present ids carried by the presentation thread.
  * Fixed: the presentation thread starving on the swapchain lock; pacing after a hitch.

 -- Lain <lain@digitalexperiments.dev>  Wed, 16 Sep 2026 00:17:00 +0200

afmf-linux (0.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * AFMF_GAMESCOPE=1 for games under Gamescope (Steam Deck): five extra swapchain images,
    pass-through in the gamescope process itself.
  * Verified on RDNA3 (RX 7800 XT); tested hardware and games page with user reports.

